{"skill":{"slug":"literature-review","displayName":"Literature Review"},"version":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1769256891795,"changelog":"Major stability and feature update by Claude Opus: added PubMed abstracts, DOI deduplication, safer date handling, and robust error handling.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3854,"sha256":"c2f51919e7a65e36fb47a18dc09c451f59e046121c51e6bbcc002abfa9167b04","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/lit_search.py","size":15433,"sha256":"e35af1f1e4c7231156e05ac9d1075b14bdf4c4a94e9114c4832d9b32f082435e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2228,"sha256":"ae04e4d00055981e433ac04e7b46e1cd458ddcb3e0074e3be96ac4b68539f3a1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789017416832,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5ffabf4988caaeec8d2a5953fe793fc9f057db099dd35c34b98518f9f5df773b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5ffabf4988caaeec8d2a5953fe793fc9f057db099dd35c34b98518f9f5df773b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: literature-review\nVersion: 1.2.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It provides a tool for searching academic databases (Semantic Scholar, OpenAlex, Crossref, PubMed) via their public APIs. The `scripts/lit_search.py` script uses environment variables (`SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY`, `OPENALEX_API_KEY`, `USER_EMAIL`, `CLAWDBOT_EMAIL`) for legitimate API authentication and identification, not for exfiltration. All network requests are directed to the stated academic API endpoints. There is no evidence of malicious execution, data exfiltration to unauthorized destinations, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts in `SKILL.md`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159879345},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":37,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789017416832},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward literature-search helper that uses disclosed academic APIs and does not show hidden persistence, destructive actions, or unrelated data access.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script reads USER_EMAIL or CLAWDBOT_EMAIL for API politeness and optional academic API keys for rate limits, which is disclosed and proportionate for the integrations.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install hook, package installer, tool replacement, or background setup was present in the inspected artifact set.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are limited to user-directed search and review workflows; scanner concern about autonomous deletion appears to come from deduplication wording, not destructive behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, local indexing, file mutation, credential-store access, or scheduled/background execution was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is academic literature review support, and the artifact implements searches/details through Semantic Scholar, OpenAlex, Crossref, and PubMed with citation metadata and abstracts.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Installers should understand that literature search terms, and possibly the configured polite-contact email or optional API keys, are sent to academic provider APIs. Avoid using sensitive private research queries if that provider exposure is unacceptable.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The skill uses network APIs and environment variables, but the destinations and env vars are documented in SKILL.md and implemented consistently in the script; absence of a formal allowed-tools block is a documentation gap, not a material Review concern here.\n[EA2] expected: The cited text refers to automatic duplicate removal in search results, not deletion of user data or autonomous high-impact decisions, so this finding is downgraded.\n[E1] expected: Requests to Semantic Scholar and other academic APIs are the core disclosed capability of the skill; no unrelated transmission or hidden endpoint was observed.\n[E1] expected: Crossref access is disclosed in the skill purpose and used for bibliographic metadata lookup; no secret or local data exfiltration path was found beyond user-provided search terms and polite-contact headers.\n[TT2] expected: The PubMed esearch-to-efetch flow passes returned PubMed IDs back to PubMed to fetch abstracts, which is normal for that API workflow and not evidence of unsafe external relay.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789017416832}}}}}